<SiteLayout title="Privacy Policy — NightGuildBot"><div class="container docs-shell"><aside class="sidebar"><div class="sidebar-label">SITE INFORMATION</div><a href="terms.html">Terms of use</a><a class="active" href="privacy.html">Privacy policy</a><a href="docs/index.html">Documentation</a></aside><article class="doc-content"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR DATA</span><h1>Privacy <span class="gradient">policy.</span></h1><p class="doc-intro">An overview of information NightGuildBot may process to make its features work.</p><p><strong>Last updated: 21 October 2026</strong></p><div class="doc-callout warning"><strong>Please review before publishing.</strong> Confirm this page against the actual database, logs, hosting provider and integrations.</div><h2>Information processed</h2><p>Depending on enabled features, NightGuildBot may process Discord user IDs, server IDs, usernames or display names, guild membership and progression, currency balances, inventory and fishing records, command usage and settings. Discord may provide message or interaction content when a command needs it.</p><h2>Why it is used</h2><p>Information is used to respond to commands, maintain game progress and settings, manage guild features, prevent abuse, troubleshoot errors and operate the bot. The bot should never need your Discord password.</p><h2>Storage and providers</h2><p>Data may be stored in the bot database and operational logs on the hosting machine or service. Discord, music integrations and hosting providers may process information required to provide their services.</p><h2>Retention and deletion</h2><p>Some records need to remain stored so balances, guilds and collections continue to work. Backups and logs may also retain records. Document a clear retention period and deletion process for the live service.</p><h2>Your choices and contact</h2><p>You can stop using the bot or remove it from a server. Publish a working contact method for questions or requests about account data, and ensure requests can be handled.</p><h2>Changes</h2><p>This policy may change when features, hosting or data storage change. NightGuildBot is an independent project and is not operated by Discord.</p></article></div></SiteLayout>